letters.body:
Dear {hero},
Today I fell down the Long Drop, landed on a Golem, and was declared the winner. Luck is a muscle. Mine is enormous. Yours will be too, I expect. It skips a generation, and your father was dreadfully careful.
{grandpa}

Dear {hero},
I have hung a rope ladder in every belly of {the_grumble}, in case you ever come looking for me. Climb it when your sack is full and your knees are wobbly. Never be too proud to go home. I always was too proud. Look where it got me: a very nice cave.
{grandpa}
